      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I assume this would work way better than chairs, right? Because now, if a moving object has chairs in it, avatars stutter A LOT.\n\nEven if it wasn't, though, this is an amazing idea.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5da66353c0be3b48ceab5ec1",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5b565300b13b3c741470153d",
        "alias": "Gray Lobster",
        "aliasID": "65c321beed6eefce4c470343",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/1618e2f2c96d78b1d49a05fb26913430.png",
        "created": "2018-07-23T22:13:20.368Z",
        "name": "Jon~",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-10-16T00:24:51.436Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 2,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d9ddfa3385d937d25f5af91",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As far as I know vrc currently syncs player position based on the global position rather than the local position, which is seen on chairs when players on moving chairs lag behind the chair itself, the way that the ik calculates the steps it needs to take would also be an issue as the avatar would be constantly trying to catch up with the players position, this isn't seen in a lot of cases like with chairs and teleporting since vrc disables locomotion for this, but disabling locomotion on the ik component would be noticeable if you want people to move around.\n\nEven with those things ignored they would still most likely have to sync what you're currently parented to so that when you get the local position it isn't updating you relative to the world or something that you used to be parented to because an RPC didn't buffer correctly or something else that would cause inconsistencies that would be very noticeable if done incorrectly.\n\nI'm not saying it shouldn't be done, a dynamic reparenting system paired with ik that calculates steps based on the gameobject's local position and syncing of the local position would be nice, but would probably take time.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
